messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 63 and 30? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo solve the math problem of finding the product of 63 and 30, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:.\n\n1. Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values:.\n   ```.\n     63.\n   x 30.\n   ----.\n   ```.\n\n2. Multiply the digit in the ones place of the bottom number (0) by each digit in the top number (63), starting from the rightmost digit:.\n   ```.\n     63.\n   x 30.\n   ----.\n     00.\n   ```.\n\n3. Since multiplying by 0 results in 0, we can simply write down 0 as the result for the ones place of the product.\n\n4. Next, move to the tens place of the bottom number (3). Multiply this digit by each digit in the top number (63), starting from the rightmost digit:.\n   ```.\n     63.\n   x 30.\n   ----.\n    189.\n   ```.\n\n5. To do this, we need to consider the place value of the digit in the top number. The digit 6 is in the tens place, so we multiply it by 3 and then shift the result one place to the left (because we're dealing with tens):.\n   ```.\n     63.\n   x 30.\n   ----.\n    189.\n   ```.\n\n6. Finally, add the results of these multiplications together. In this case, we only have one result (189), so we don't need to add anything else:.\n   ```.\n     63.\n   x 30.\n   ----.\n    1890.\n   ```.\n\nSo, the product of 63 and 30 is 1890.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
