messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 40 and 52? Please reason step by step.', '<think>.\nTo find the product of 40 and 52, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. We can break down the numbers into their factors and then multiply them separately. .\n\n40 can be broken down into 4 x 10, and 52 can be broken down into 50 + 2. .\n\nSo, the product of 40 and 52 can be calculated as follows:.\n\n(4 x 10) x (50 + 2) = (4 x 50) + (4 x 2) + (10 x 50) + (10 x 2).\n\nNow, we can calculate each of the products separately:.\n\n4 x 50 = 200.\n4 x 2 = 8.\n10 x 50 = 500.\n10 x 2 = 20.\n\nFinally, we can add all the products together:.\n\n200 + 8 + 500 + 20 = 728.\n\nTherefore, the product of 40 and 52 is 728.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
